      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's an expanded version of the guide:\n\n**Initial Setup for VortexScale Deployment Engine**\n\nTo get started with VortexScale, ensure your Linux environment meets the following system requirements:\n\n* A 64-bit kernel (preferably the latest version)\n* A compatible version of Bash scripting (available with most modern Linux distributions)\n\n**Step 1: Download and Install vortex-cli**\n\n1. Navigate to our internal repository and download the `vortex-cli` binary. The file name will be `vortex-cli_<version_name>`.\n2. Move the binary to a location of your choice, such as `~/vortex-cli`.\n\n**Step 2: Make vortex-cli Executable**\n\n1. Change the permissions of the `vortex-cli` binary to make it executable using `chmod +x vortex-cli`.\nThis step allows the `vortex-cli` command to be executed directly from the command line.\n\n**Step 3: Add vortex-cli to System Path**\n\n1. Add the `~/vortex-cli` directory to your system's system path using `export PATH=$PATH:~/vortex-cli`.\nThis allows you to run `vortex-cli` commands from any directory.\n\n**Step 4:Bootstrap VortexScale**\n\n1.",
